**Read:** [Fatal liquid nitrogen release — CSB Foundation Food Group investigation](../sources/Foundation-Food-Group-Investigation-CSB.lingua#r_7KXAYPC80QQ764WA8DKSJTDRGA), the complete investigation; [Reliability-centered maintenance — NASA, September 2008](../sources/Reliability-Centered-Maintenance-NASA.lingua#r_08ZD3ATSYCJX5586EYSY0M4N3R), failure analysis and feedback.

Preserve the as-found state, time sequence, configuration and measurement limits before fitting a cause to them. Separate a component's observed damage from the mechanism that produced it and from conditions that allowed the consequence to grow. Several mechanisms can create similar traces.

Propose tests that distinguish alternatives and record what a negative test would mean. Changing a failed assembly before preserving evidence can erase the information needed to distinguish a manufacturing defect from installation, service or intervention effects.

**Work:** Reassess the nitrogen case with an evidence table: established, inferred, contradicted and unresolved. Construct a different vacuum-service case from synthetic data, then revise its explanation after one new observation. State the limits of each causal claim.

**Return:** [Industrial gases, vacuum and high-purity supplies — from molecules to useful service](../Industrial-gases-and-vacuum.lingua#r_3GHQJEYMYEN6JDKSF4PPJ403RF).
**Continue in gas and vacuum systems:** [Handover and change preserve the meaning of the system](Handover-and-change-preserve-the-meaning-of-the-system.lingua#r_50S4H3D04PB1P1DKAYTWYNWYS1).

